The image files in this directory are the brands' own colored artwork, one
per package manager, named by the manager that shows it rather than by the
brand that drew it: pip.svg is Python's mark and cargo.svg is Rust's gear.

Where each file came from:

  brew.svg     Homebrew's logo, from homarr-labs/dashboard-icons
               (Apache-2.0 collection).
  bun.svg      Bun's logo, from selfhst/icons (CC BY 4.0).
  cargo.svg    Rust's official gear, recolored to Rust orange #F74C00: the
               path is the black logo published by SVG Logos
               (github.com/gilbarbara/logos, CC0), and the Cargo adapter is
               what builds Rust packages.
  npm.svg      npm's logo, from devicons/devicon (MIT).
  pip.svg      Python's logo, from selfhst/icons (CC BY 4.0).
  pipx.svg     pipx's mark from Simple Icons (https://simpleicons.org, CC0)
               filled with pipx's brand color #2CFFAA, as served by
               thesvg.org.
  uv-tool.svg  uv's logo, from astral-sh/uv (docs/assets/logo-letter.svg).

The icons are shown to identify the software they belong to. The marks
themselves remain the trademarks of their owners: Homebrew, Oven (Bun), the
Rust Foundation (Cargo), npm, Inc., the Python Software Foundation, pipx, and
Astral (uv).

The set is not complete. A manager without a file here shows without a mark;
add one named by the manager's ID to give it its own.
